From c7517d77ea138090fba2f74bfd98e9e5a6073887 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: qiuuuu622 <q17762079638@outlook.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 13:42:50 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] perf(gdn): SM90 mixed-length split dispatch for GDN prefill

When one sequence dominates an unsaturated varlen batch, run it through the
CP kernel on a side stream while the rest run through the non-CP kernel.
Groups are contiguous slices, so no tensors are copied. Gated on host
lengths (cu_seqlens_cpu) to avoid a device sync; disable with
FLASHINFER_GDN_SM90_SPLIT=0.

H20, Qwen3.5-122B TP4 shape (Hq=4, Hv=16, D=128), CUDA-graph device time:
8192+3x1024 0.753->0.519ms (1.45x), 16384+3x1024 1.500->0.884ms (1.70x),
32768+3x1024 2.999->1.605ms (1.87x). Gate fitted on 54 shapes: every accepted
case >=1.11x, every rejected case <=1.02x.

AI-assisted.
